    {
      "id": "c4a92809-6911-4f11-b69e-c3626b75050b",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview & setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -896,
        -464
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 780,
        "height": 2136,
        "content": "# Generate SEO content with Perplexity and GPT-5 for WordPress\n# 📥  [Open full documentation on Notion](https://automatisation.notion.site/Course-Generate-SEO-content-with-Perplexity-and-GPT-5-for-WordPress-3a03d6550fd9817f9752dbe45c942969)\n\n## How it works\nThe workflow reads a content idea from a Google Sheet, researches it live with Perplexity so the facts are current, then writes an SEO-friendly title, meta description, slug and full HTML body with GPT-5 in a single structured call (no manual JSON parsing). It publishes the article to WordPress with the status you configured, generates a photorealistic cover image with DALL-E, uploads it to the media library, sets it as the featured image, and finally writes the post ID back to the sheet so the idea is never processed twice.\n\nCanvas map, left to right:\n1. Trigger & configuration\n2. Read the content plan\n3. Research & write\n4. Publish & cover image\n5. Track what was published\n\n## Setup\n1. Create a Google Sheet with the columns `DATE`, `PROMPT`, `TITLE`, `ID POST`. Fill only `PROMPT` with your topic ideas.\n2. Select that spreadsheet and tab on the two **Google Sheets** nodes.\n3. Open **Configuration** and set `wordpress_site_url` to your own domain, then adjust the models, image settings, word count range, language and publish status.\n4. Select your OpenAI credential on the two **OpenAI Model** sub-nodes and on **Generate Cover Image with DALL-E**.\n5. Select your Perplexity credential on **Research Topic with Perplexity**, and your WordPress credential on the WordPress node and the two HTTP Request nodes.\n6. Run the workflow manually to test, then swap the manual trigger for a Schedule Trigger to run it on autopilot.\n\n## Requirements\n- OpenAI API key (text model + DALL-E image generation)\n- Perplexity API key\n- A WordPress site with the REST API enabled and an application password\n- A Google Sheet used as the content plan\n\n## Customization\n- Every shared value lives in the **Configuration** node: text model, image size, quality and style, word count range, Perplexity recency window, output language, WordPress domain and publish status.\n- Set `wordpress_post_status` to `publish` if you want articles to go live directly instead of staying as drafts.\n- Edit the system message of **Write Article and Title** to change the tone, structure or length of the article.\n- Add a filter on **Get Unprocessed Idea** (for example `ID POST` is empty) to only pick up rows that were never published.\n\nAI writes the first draft: review the article in WordPress before publishing it.\n\n---\nNeed help customizing?\nContact me for consulting and support : [Linkedin](https://www.linkedin.com/in/doctor-firass/)\n\n# MY NEW YOUTUBE CHANNEL\n👉 [Subscribe to my new YouTube channel](https://www.youtube.com/@DrFiras_AI). Here I'll share videos and Shorts with practical tutorials and FREE templates for n8n.\n\n[![The AI Doctor](https://www.dr-firas.com/the-ai-doctor.png)](https://www.youtube.com/@DrFiras_AI)"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
